# Backend environment (`~/.ssh/be/.env`)

Runtime config for the Node backend is loaded from **`~/.ssh/be/.env`** (not committed to git). After changes, restart PM2: `pm2 restart onlinemallwebsite`.

Relevant loader: `be/loadEnv.js` (imported first in `be/server_be.js`) → `be/utils/expandHomeEnv.js` (dotenv + dotenv-expand, `override: true`).

**Source of this doc:** Ubuntu production copy **`myscript/ubuntu/be.env`** (gitignored — real secrets). Refresh it from xbox2 with the Mac function **`syncbenv`** (`source ~/b`). Values below are **production** unless marked **Mac**. **Secrets are redacted** (`****`) — real values only in `~/.ssh/be/.env` / `myscript/ubuntu/be.env`, never in git or rules.

## Parsing rules (dotenv)

- **Duplicate keys → last one wins.** Prod file repeats `ROOT_FOLDER` (`/home/lawsen0` then `/mnt/pgdata16` → **`/mnt/pgdata16`**), `AI_VOICE` (`Sora` then **`Sulafat`**), `GEMINI_API_KEY`, `FE_RATE_LIMIT_ENABLE`, `USB_ICON_ENCRYPTTON`, `ENABLE_LOGIN_BYPASS`.
- **Must be `KEY=value`.** `KEY:value` (no space after `:`) is **silently ignored**.
- Inline comments after whitespace are stripped (`REFRESH_ASN_VPN_AT=24   # default` → `24`).
- `${VAR}` expansion works (`FAST_STORAGE_FOLDER=${ROOT_FOLDER}/…`).
- Keys are **case-sensitive** on Linux.
- Mac: `loadEnv.js` replaces unwritable `/mnt/…` storage paths with `~/onlinemallwebsite_storage` / `~/onlinemallwebsite_largecheapstorage`.

## Known problems in current prod `be.env`

| Line in prod | Effect | Fix |
|---|---|---|
| `FLORISTONE_API_Key:292711`, `FLORISTONE_PASSWORD:****` | Colon syntax → **not loaded**; send-flowers has no credentials on prod. | Use `FLORISTONE_API_Key=…` / `FLORISTONE_PASSWORD=…`. |
| `Admin=` / `DemoUser=` / `PilotUser=` / `Public=` | `be/mallDepartmentMode.js` reads **uppercase** keys only → ignored → every category gets `show_all` (PUBLIC not restricted). | Rename to `ADMIN=`, `DEMOUSER=`, `PILOTUSER=`, `PUBLIC=`. |
| `AUTO_UI_POST_UPDATET=false` | Typo → ignored → post auto-update stays **on** (default `true`). | `AUTO_UI_POST_UPDATE=false`. |
| `LINKEDIN_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:3000/…` | Prod LinkedIn OAuth would redirect to localhost. | `https://onlinemall.website/api/auth/linkedin/callback` (and add it in LinkedIn app). |
| `DEBUG_PHOTO_INFO=true`, `MOBILE_PHOTO_UPLOAD_DEBUG=true` | Debug UI / logging on in production. | `false` unless actively debugging. |

**Keys in prod with no code reader (dead config):** `DISABLE_USEDRIVE`, `ALBUM_BUTTON_FONT_SIZE`, `USB_ICON_ENCRYPTTON`, `NOTES_/PHOTOALBUMS_TOTAL_{FREE,LEVEL1,LEVEL2}_TRANSFER_MB`, `RECORD_NOTES_MAX_IMAGE_SIZE_MB`, `RECORD_NOTES_MAX_IMAGE_PER_ACCOUNT`, `NOTES_/PHOTOALBUMS_POSTGRES`, `NOTES_/PHOTOALBUMS_GOOGLE_DRIVE`, `NOTES_/PHOTOALBUMS_DROPBOX`, `DROPBOX_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID/SECRET`, `DROPBOX_VAULT_REDIRECT_URI`, `RECORD_NOTES_USB_MODE`, `RECORD_PHOTOALBUMS_USB_MODE`, `PHOTOALBUMS_BACKUP_USB_DISABLE`.

## Security / platform (Mac vs Ubuntu differ)

```bash
# Ubuntu production
NODE_ENV=production
AUTH_COOKIE_SAMESITE=strict
AUTH_COOKIE_SECURE=true
PUBLIC_APP_URL=https://onlinemall.website
JWT_PRIVATE_KEY_PATH=${HOME}/.ssh/be/private_key.pem
JWT_PUBLIC_KEY_PATH=${HOME}/.ssh/be/public_key.pem
CLUSTER_MULTI_SERVER=true
REDIS_URL=redis://:****@127.0.0.1:6379
```

| Variable | Prod | Mac dev | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| `NODE_ENV` | `production` | `development` | |
| `AUTH_COOKIE_SECURE` | `true` | `false` | `true` behind HAProxy HTTPS. |
| `PUBLIC_APP_URL` | `https://onlinemall.website` | `http://localhost:3000` | |
| `DEV_ALLOWED_ORIGINS` | unset | `http://localhost:3000,http://localhost:40000` | **Mac only** CORS list (`be/server_be.js`). |
| `JWT_*_KEY_PATH` | `${HOME}/.ssh/be/*.pem` | `/Users/a/.ssh/be/*.pem` | RS256 pair; not in repo. |
| `CLUSTER_MULTI_SERVER` | `true` | unset | Strict startup checks that media / OneDrive staging use shared storage (`be/utils/sharedMediaStorage.js`, `*OneDriveStagingRoot.js`). |
| `REDIS_URL` | password-protected localhost | `redis://localhost:6379` | Shared Redis for all web hosts. Always TTL; fall back to DB if down. |

## Storage folders

```bash
ROOT_FOLDER=/mnt/pgdata16
FAST_STORAGE_FOLDER=${ROOT_FOLDER}/onlinemallwebsite_storage
UPLOAD_FOLDER=${FAST_STORAGE_FOLDER}/mobile_upload
TUTADATES_PHOTO_FOLDER=${FAST_STORAGE_FOLDER}/photos/
TUTADATES_VIDEO_FOLDER=${FAST_STORAGE_FOLDER}/videos/
RECORD_NOTES_FOLDER=${FAST_STORAGE_FOLDER}/notes/
LARGE_CHEAP_STORAGE_FOLDER=${ROOT_FOLDER}/onlinemallwebsite_largecheapstorage
INCLUDE_USB_DMG_EXE=false
USB_DMG_EXE=${FAST_STORAGE_FOLDER}/USB_DMG_EXE
```

| Variable | Notes |
|---|---|
| `ROOT_FOLDER` | Base for expansions. Mac: `FAST_STORAGE_FOLDER=/Users/a/onlinemallwebsite_storage`, `LARGE_CHEAP_STORAGE_FOLDER=/Users/a/onlinemallwebsite_largecheapstorage`. |
| `FAST_STORAGE_FOLDER` | General app storage and **Tuta Dates media**: `{root}/users/M{member_id}/tutadates/{photos,videos}`. |
| `UPLOAD_FOLDER` | Phone/mobile upload staging (`photoAlbumsMobileUploadFolderRoutes.js`). |
| `TUTADATES_PHOTO_FOLDER` / `TUTADATES_VIDEO_FOLDER` | **Legacy** flat roots, read fallback only. New uploads → per-member folders above. |
| `RECORD_NOTES_FOLDER` | Legacy notes root (`deleteMemberMobileUploads.js`, `tutaMallUserBackup.js`). |
| `LARGE_CHEAP_STORAGE_FOLDER` | TutaDrive / TutaNotes / TutaPhoto vaults: `{root}/users/M{member_id}/notes` and `…/photoalbums`. **Multi-server: every web host must see the same path** (vault coherence, `vaultClusterCoherence.js`). Migration helper: `node be/scripts/migrateTutaDatesMediaToMemberFolders.js --dry-run`. |
| `INCLUDE_USB_DMG_EXE` / `USB_DMG_EXE` | USB bridge installer bundling + download dir (`includeUsbDmgExeConfig.js`, `photoAlbumsBridgeInstaller.js`). Prod `false`. |

