## TutaPhoto free-tier quotas

```bash
TUTAPHOTO_MAX_SIZE_IMAGE_UPLOAD_MB=20
TUTAPHOTO_MAX_SIZE_VIDEO_UPLOAD_MB=100
TUTAPHOTO_MAX_IMAGE_PER_ACCOUNT=1000
TUTAPHOTO_MAX_VIDEO_PER_ACCOUNT=100
```

| Variable | Behavior |
|---|---|
| `TUTAPHOTO_MAX_SIZE_IMAGE_UPLOAD_MB` | Per-image cap. Oversized images auto-downsized in the browser (JPEG re-encode) with a popup; if that fails, user is told to resize externally. |
| `TUTAPHOTO_MAX_SIZE_VIDEO_UPLOAD_MB` | Per-video cap. Browsers cannot transcode → oversized video refused ("Auto downsize failed"). |
| `TUTAPHOTO_MAX_IMAGE_PER_ACCOUNT` / `…_VIDEO_…` | Total live images / videos per account across all albums. |

Read by `be/utils/tutaPhotoQuotaConfig.js`; counts come from the member vault (`note_attachments`). Exposed at `GET /api/photoAlbums/mediaQuota`, enforced again in `POST /api/photoAlbums/notes/:noteId/attachments`. `be/server_be.js` raises the JSON body ceiling to `ceil(largest cap × 4/3) + 8` MiB (142 MiB at these values).

