## Mac-only remote-access secrets (not in prod `be.env`)

```bash
MAC_SUDO_PASSWORD=****          # sudo prompt for scripts/deploy-ssh-mac.sh
SSH_KEY_PASSPHRASE=****         # corruptedKey_march2024 passphrase
UBUNTU_POSTGRES_PASSWORD=****   # Ubuntu test_user1 — scripts/ubuntu-psql.sh
```

Only in the **Mac** `~/.ssh/be/.env`. Used by the SSH / remote-psql helpers (see `ssh.mdc`), not by app code. The Node backend loads them into its environment, but the `MAC_` / `SSH_` / `UBUNTU_` prefixes are not on the Vite `envPrefix` list, so they never reach the FE bundle.

## When changing these

1. Edit `~/.ssh/be/.env` on the target machine (Mac and Ubuntu copies differ — see tables above).
2. Ubuntu: `pm2 restart onlinemallwebsite`. Mac: restart the Node process (`beall`).
3. Keys mirrored into the FE bundle (`FE_RATE_*`, `SPECIAL_*`, `PRICE_PER_TOKEN`, `SELF_INTRO_VIDEO_MAX_LENGTH`, `*_VIDEO_TUTORIAL`, `SPEEDDATING`, `RAG_UI_ENABLED`, `ALBUM_BINDER_WIDTH_PCT`, …): restart Vite on Mac / rebuild FE on prod.
4. `SERVERDOWN_TEXT` / `ALARM_USB_VOL` / `SITE_UPTIME_SMS_TO`: `sudo systemctl restart site-uptime-monitor` on Ubuntu.
5. After editing prod, run **`syncbenv`** on Mac to refresh `myscript/ubuntu/be.env`, then update this doc.

